'outlook' aria-label='Next hours in London'><li><span class='muted'>11:00</span><svg class='i' role='img' aria-label='Rain'><use href='#i-rain'/></svg><b>9°</b></li><li><span class='muted'>13:00</span><svg class='i' role='img' aria-label='Showers'><use href='#i-drizzle'/></svg><b>10°</b></li><li><span class='muted'>16:00</span><svg class='i' role='img' aria-label='Cloudy'><use href='#i-cloud'/></svg><b>10°</b></li><li><span class='muted'>19:00</span><svg class='i' role='img' aria-label='Cloudy'><use href='#i-cloud'/></svg><b>9°</b></li></ol></article><article class='card cmp' data-testid='compare-card' aria-label='Perth'><div class='wx-band' data-wx='hot-day'><span class='small' style='font-weight:600'>Hot and sunny, day</span><svg class='i i-lg' aria-hidden='true'><use href='#i-sun'/></svg></div><div class='cmp-head'><h2>Perth</h2><p class='small muted' style='margin:0'>Western Australia, Australia · 18:40</p><p class='cmp-temp' data-testid='compare-temperature-count'>34°</p><p style='margin:4px 0 0;font-weight:600'>Sunny and hot</p></div><dl class='cmp-stats'><div><dt>Feels like</dt><dd>35°</dd></div><div><dt>Wind</dt><dd>19 km/h SW</dd></div><div><dt>Humidity</dt><dd>22%</dd></div><div><dt>High / low</dt><dd>38° / 21°</dd></div></dl><ol class='outlook' aria-label='Next hours in Perth'><li><span class='muted'>19:00</span><svg class='i' role='img' aria-label='Sunny'><use href='#i-moon'/></svg><b>34°</b></li><li><span class='muted'>21:00</span><svg class='i' role='img' aria-label='Sunny'><use href='#i-moon'/></svg><b>30°</b></li><li><span class='muted'>00:00</span><svg class='i' role='img' aria-label='Sunny'><use href='#i-moon'/></svg><b>23°</b></li><li><span class='muted'>03:00</span><svg class='i' role='img' aria-label='Sunny'><use href='#i-moon'/></svg><b>21°</b></li></ol></article><article class='card cmp' data-testid='compare-card' aria-label='Oslo'><div class='wx-band' data-wx='snow-day'><span class='small' style='font-weight:600'>Heavy snow, day</span><svg class='i i-lg' aria-hidden='true'><use href='#i-snow'/></svg></div><div class='cmp-head'><h2>Oslo</h2><p class='small muted' style='margin:0'>Oslo, Norway · 11:40</p><p class='cmp-temp' data-testid='compare-temperature-count'>−3°</p><p style='margin:4px 0 0;font-weight:600'>Heavy snow</p></div><dl class='cmp-stats'><div><dt>Feels like</dt><dd>−8°</dd></div><div><dt>Wind</dt><dd>14 km/h N</dd></div><div><dt>Humidity</dt><dd>88%</dd></div><div><dt>High / low</dt><dd>−2° / −7°</dd></div></dl><ol class='outlook' aria-label='Next hours in Oslo'><li><span class='muted'>12:00</span><svg class='i' role='img' aria-label='Heavy snow'><use href='#i-snow'/></svg><b>−3°</b></li><li><span class='muted'>14:00</span><svg class='i' role='img' aria-label='Heavy snow'><use href='#i-snow'/></svg><b>−2°</b></li><li><span class='muted'>17:00</span><svg class='i' role='img' aria-label='Flurries'><use href='#i-snow'/></svg><b>−2°</b></li><li><span class='muted'>20:00</span><svg class='i' role='img' aria-label='Flurries'><use href='#i-snow'/></svg><b>−4°</b></li></ol></article><article class='card cmp' data-testid='compare-card' aria-label='Sydney'><div class='wx-band' data-wx='clear-night'><span class='small' style='font-weight:600'>Clear sky, night</span><svg class='i i-lg' aria-hidden='true'><use href='#i-moon'/></svg></div><div class='cmp-head'><h2>Sydney</h2><p class='small muted' style='margin:0'>New South Wales, Australia · 21:40</p><p class='cmp-temp' data-testid='compare-temperature-count'>22°</p><p style='margin:4px 0 0;font-weight:600'>Clear</p></div><dl class='cmp-stats'><div><dt>Feels like</dt><dd>22°</dd></div><div><dt>Wind</dt><dd>11 km/h NE</dd></div><div><dt>Humidity</dt><dd>68%</dd></div><div><dt>High / low</dt><dd>27° / 20°</dd></div></dl><ol class='outlook' aria-label='Next hours in Sydney'><li><span class='muted'>22:00</span><svg class='i' role='img' aria-label='Clear'><use href='#i-moon'/></svg><b>23°</b></li><li><span class='muted'>00:00</span><svg class='i' role='img' aria-label='Clear'><use href='#i-moon'/></svg><b>21°</b></li><li><span class='muted'>03:00</span><svg class='i' role='img' aria-label='Clear'><use href='#i-moon'/></svg><b>20°</b></li><li><span class='muted'>06:00</span><svg class='i' role='img' aria-label='Clear'><use href='#i-sun'/></svg><b>21°</b></li></ol></article></div><p class='small muted' style='margin:0'>Up to 4 cities. Each card is tinted to its own weather. On a phone, swipe sideways.</p></div></div>\\n<div data-state=\\\"empty\\\" data-testid='compare-empty'><div class='scene' data-wx='calm' aria-hidden='true'><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><div class='stack gap-4 narrow'><div class='screen-header' style='margin-bottom:0'><h1 data-testid='compare-title'>Compare</h1></div><section class='card empty' data-testid='compare-empty-card'><svg class='i i-lg' aria-hidden='true'><use href='#i-compare'/></svg><h2>Pick at least two cities</h2><p>Tick 2 to 4 of your saved cities to see their weather side by side.</p><a class='button' href='#/cities' data-testid='compare-pick-link'>Choose cities</a></section></div></div>\\n</section>\\n<section data-screen=\\\"settings\\\" data-testid='screen-settings' aria-label='Settings'>\\n<div data-state=\\\"populated\\\" data-testid='settings-populated'><div class='scene' data-wx='rain-day' aria-hidden='true'><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><div class='stack gap-4 narrow'><div class='screen-header' style='margin-bottom:0'><div class='stack gap-1'><h1 data-testid='settings-title'>Settings</h1><p class='muted' style='margin:0'>Changes save straight away, in this browser.</p></div><button type='button' class='button' data-open='install-dialog' data-testid='settings-install-button'><svg class='i' aria-hidden='true'><use href='#i-download'/></svg>Install app</button></div><section class='card' aria-label='Units'><div class='setting-row'><div><h2>Units</h2><p class='muted'>Changes every temperature in the app. °C shows wind in km/h and rain in mm; °F shows mph and inches.</p></div><div class='unit-toggle' role='group' aria-label='Temperature units' data-toggle-group><button type='button' class='filter-chip' aria-pressed='true' data-testid='settings-celsius-button'>°C</button><button type='button' class='filter-chip' aria-pressed='false' data-toast='toast-units' data-testid='settings-fahrenheit-button'>°F</button></div></div></section><section class='card stack gap-4' aria-label='Effects and motion'><h2>Effects and motion</h2><div class='setting-row'><div><b>Simpler effects</b><p class='muted'>Fewer raindrops, flakes and clouds. Kinder to older phones and battery. Each kind of weather still looks different.</p></div><input type='checkbox' role='switch' class='switch' aria-label='Simpler effects' data-testid='settings-effects-checkbox'></div><div class='setting-row'><div><b>Reduced motion</b><p class='muted'>Set by your device. When it asks for less motion, scenes hold still: the weather shows through colour and soft shapes, with no falling, flashing or shimmering.</p></div><span class='badge' data-testid='settings-motion-status'>Your device: full motion</span></div><div class='setting-row'><div><b>Automatic smoothness</b><p class='muted'>If your device struggles, the app quietly lightens the scene, and brings detail back when it can.</p></div><span class='badge badge-success'>Always on</span></div></section><section class='card' aria-label='Location'><div class='setting-row'><div><h2>Location</h2><p class='muted'>Used only to fetch your local weather. Tap to check where you are again.</p></div><button type='button' class='button button-outline' data-toast='toast-locate' data-testid='settings-locate-button'><svg class='i' aria-hidden='true'><use href='#i-locate'/></svg>Use my location</button></div></section><section class='card stack gap-2' aria-label='Saved in this browser'><h2>Saved in this browser</h2><p class='muted' style='margin:0' data-testid='settings-browser-note'>Your saved cities, units and effects choice live only in this browser on this device. There's no account and nothing is sent to us. If you clear your browser's data, they'll be gone and you'll need to add your cities again.</p></section><section class='card stack gap-3' aria-label='The scenes'><h2>The scenes</h2><p class='muted' style='margin:0'>Each kind of weather has a day and a night look, timed by sunrise and sunset in the city you're viewing.</p><ul class='swatches' data-testid='settings-scene-list'><li class='swatch' data-wx='clear-day'><span><svg class='i' aria-hidden='true'><use href='#i-sun'/></svg></span><span>Clear, day</span></li><li class='swatch' data-wx='clear-night'><span><svg class='i' aria-hidden='true'><use href='#i-moon'/></svg></span><span>Clear, night</span></li><li class='swatch' data-wx='hot-day'><span><svg class='i' aria-hidden='true'><use href='#i-sun'/></svg></span><span>Hot, day</span></li><li class='swatch' data-wx='hot-night'><span><svg class='i' aria-hidden='true'><use href='#i-moon'/></svg></span><span>Hot, night</span></li><li class='swatch' data-wx='cloudy-day'><span><svg class='i' aria-hidden='true'><use href='#i-cloud'/></svg></span><span>Cloudy, day</span></li><li class='swatch' data-wx='cloudy-night'><span><svg class='i' aria-hidden='true'><use href='#i-cloud'/></svg></span><span>Cloudy, night</span></li><li class='swatch' data-wx='rain-day'><span><svg class='i' aria-hidden='true'><use href='#i-rain'/></svg></span><span>Rain, day</span></li><li class='swatch' data-wx='rain-night'><span><svg class='i' aria-hidden='true'><use href='#i-rain'/></svg></span><span>Rain, night</span></li><li class='swatch' data-wx='storm-day'><span><svg class='i' aria-hidden='true'><use href='#i-storm'/></svg></span><span>Storm, day</span></li><li class='swatch' data-wx='storm-night'><span><svg class='i' aria-hidden='true'><use href='#i-storm'/></svg></span><span>Storm, night</span></li><li class='swatch' data-wx='snow-day'><span><svg class='i' aria-hidden='true'><use href='#i-snow'/></svg></span><span>Snow, day</span></li><li class='swatch' data-wx='snow-night'><span><svg class='i' aria-hidden='true'><use href='#i-snow'/></svg></span><span>Snow, night</span></li><li class='swatch' data-wx='wind-day'><span><svg class='i' aria-hidden='true'><use href='#i-wind'/></svg></span><span>Wind, day</span></li><li class='swatch' data-wx='wind-night'><span><svg class='i' aria-hidden='true'><use href='#i-wind'/></svg></span><span>Wind, night</span></li><li class='swatch' data-wx='fog-day'><span><svg class='i' aria-hidden='true'><use href='#i-fog'/></svg></span><span>Fog, day</span></li><li class='swatch' data-wx='fog-night'><span><svg class='i' aria-hidden='true'><use href='#i-fog'/></svg></span><span>Fog, night</span></li></ul></section><p class='small muted' style='margin:0'>Weather and city search by Open-Meteo.</p></div></div>\\n</section>\\n      </main>\\n      <dialog class='dialog' id='install-dialog' aria-labelledby='install-title' data-testid='install-dialog'><div class='stack gap-4'><h2 id='install-title'>Put the weather on your home screen</h2><p class='muted' style='margin:0'>Installed, it opens full screen like any other app. No app store, no sign-in, and your cities stay in this browser.</p><div class='form-actions'><button type='button' class='button button-outline' data-close data-testid='install-cancel-button'>Not now</button><button type='button' class='button' data-close data-toast='toast-install' data-testid='install-confirm-button'><svg class='i' aria-hidden='true'><use href='#i-download'/></svg>Install</button></div></div></dialog>\\n      <div class=\\\"toaster\\\"><div class='toast' id='toast-units' role='status' data-open='false' data-testid='toast-units'>Showing °F. Wind is now in mph and rain in inches.</div><div class='toast' id='toast-refreshed' role='status' data-open='false' data-testid='toast-refreshed'>Weather updated just now.</div><div class='toast' id='toast-locate' role='status' data-open='false' data-testid='toast-locate'>Checking your location…</div><div class='toast' id='toast-locate-blocked' role='status' data-open='false' data-testid='toast-locate-blocked'>Location is still blocked. Allow it in your browser's settings, then try again.</div><div class='toast' id='toast-saved' role='status' data-open='false' data-testid='toast-saved'>Springfield saved to your places.</div><div class='toast' id='toast-removed' role='status' data-open='false' data-testid='toast-removed'>City removed. <button type='button' class='button button-ghost' data-toast='toast-undo' data-testid='toast-undo-button'>Undo</button></div><div class='toast' id='toast-undo' role='status' data-open='false' data-testid='toast-undo'>City put back.</div><div class='toast' id='toast-retry' role='status' data-open='false' data-testid='toast-retry'>Trying again…</div><div class='toast' id='toast-install' role='status' data-open='false' data-testid='toast-install'>Installing. The app will open from your home screen.</div></div>\\n    </div>\\n    <script>\\n      // Mockup only: the pressed unit becomes the selected one in its group.\\n      document.addEventListener(\\\"click\\\", (e) => {\\n        const b = e.target.closest(\\\"[data-toggle-group] > button\\\");\\n        if (!b) return;\\n        for (const s of b.parentElement.children) s.setAttribute(\\\"aria-pressed\\\", String(s === b));\\n      });\\n    </script>\\n    <script>\\n      (() => {\\n        const screens = [...document.querySelectorAll(\\\"[data-screen]\\\")];\\n\\n        function route() {\\n          const [name, state] = location.hash.replace(/^#\\\\/?/, \\\"\\\").split(\\\"/\\\");\\n          const target =\\n            screens.find((s) => s.dataset.screen === name) ?? screens[0];\\n          for (const screen of screens) screen.hidden = screen !== target;\\n\\n          const states = [...target.querySelectorAll(\\\":scope > [data-state]\\\")];\\n          const names = states.map((s) => s.dataset.state);\\n          const shown = names.includes(state)\\n            ? state\\n            : names.includes(\\\"populated\\\")\\n              ? \\\"populated\\\"\\n              : names[0];\\n          for (const el of states) el.hidden = el.dataset.state !== shown;\\n\\n          for (const link of document.querySelectorAll(\\n            '[data-testid^=\\\"nav-\\\"]',\\n          )) {\\n            const linked = link\\n              .getAttribute(\\\"href\\\")\\n              .replace(/^#\\\\/?/, \\\"\\\")\\n              .split(\\\"/\\\")[0];\\n            if (linked === target.dataset.screen)\\n              link.setAttribute(\\\"aria-current\\\", \\\"page\\\");\\n            else link.removeAttribute(\\\"aria-current\\\");\\n          }\\n          document\\n            .querySelector(\\\"[data-menu-toggle]\\\")\\n            ?.setAttribute(\\\"aria-expanded\\\", \\\"false\\\");\\n          window.scrollTo(0, 0);\\n        }\\n\\n        document.addEventListener(\\\"click\\\", (event) => {\\n          const opener = event.target.closest(\\\"[data-open]\\\");\\n          if (opener) document.getElementById(opener.dataset.open)?.showModal();\\n\\n          const closer = event.target.closest(\\\"[data-close]\\\");\\n          if (closer) closer.closest(\\\"dialog\\\")?.close();\\n\\n          const pressed = event.target.closest(\\\"[aria-pressed]\\\");\\n          if (pressed)\\n            pressed.setAttribute(\\n              \\\"aria-pressed\\\",\\n              String(pressed.getAttribute(\\\"aria-pressed\\\") !== \\\"true\\\"),\\n            );\\n\\n          const tab = event.target.closest(\\\"[role=tab]\\\");\\n          if (tab)\\n            for (const sibling of tab.parentElement.querySelectorAll(\\n              \\\":scope > [role=tab]\\\",\\n            ))\\n              sibling.setAttribute(\\\"aria-selected\\\", String(sibling === tab));\\n\\n          const menu = event.target.closest(\\\"[data-menu-toggle]\\\");\\n          if (menu)\\n            menu.setAttribute(\\n              \\\"aria-expanded\\\",\\n              String(menu.getAttribute(\\\"aria-expanded\\\") !== \\\"true\\\"),\\n            );\\n\\n          const toaster = event.target.closest(\\\"[data-toast]\\\");\\n          if (toaster) {\\n            const toast = document.getElementById(toaster.dataset.toast);\\n            toast.dataset.open = \\\"true\\\";\\n            clearTimeout(toast.timer);\\n            toast.timer = setTimeout(() => {\\n              toast.dataset.open = \\\"false\\\";\\n            }, 4000);\\n          }\\n\\n          if (event.target.closest(\\\"[data-theme-toggle]\\\")) {\\n            const root = document.documentElement;\\n            const dark =\\n              root.classList.contains(\\\"dark\\\") ||\\n              (!root.classList.contains(\\\"light\\\") &&\\n                matchMedia(\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\").matches);\\n            root.classList.toggle(\\\"dark\\\", !dark);\\n            root.classList.toggle(\\\"light\\\", dark);\\n          }\\n        });\\n\\n        addEventListener(\\\"hashchange\\\", route);\\n        route();\\n      })();\\n    </script>\\n  </body>\\n</html>\\n\"}"}}]},"finish_reason":null}]}

data: {"choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"index":2,"id":"des_write_doc","function":{"name":"write_file","arguments":""}}]},"finish_reason":null}]}

data: {"choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"index":2,"function":{"arguments":"{\"path\":\".builder/DESIGN.md\",\"content\":\"# Animated Weather design\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nAnimated Weather is a browser app for people who check the weather often, on a phone or a desktop. The whole screen is a moving scene of the weather where you are, or in a city you pick. Under the scene sit the usual tools: your location, saved cities, °C/°F, a 24-hour and 7-day forecast, and a side-by-side comparison of 2 to 4 cities. There is no sign-in, and everything is kept in the browser.\\n\\nMockup: `.builder/designs/index.html`. Open it from disk. Routes are `#/screen/state`, for example `#/home/storm` or `#/search/empty`.\\n\\n## Theme\\n\\n- The person's words for the look and feel: \\\"Modern and sleek base: crisp neutrals, system sans-serif, generous whitespace, subtle depth, with frosted soft panels over the scene. The accent and background palette shift per weather condition and day/night (warm amber for hot, slate blue for rain, deep indigo for night). Layout reflows between phone and desktop.\\\"\\n- Theme: the kit's neutral theme, changed for the **Adaptive weather-driven** design concept.\\n- Changes:\\n  - `--card` and `--popover` are translucent white (day) or translucent indigo (night), and every `.card`, `.stat-grid-item`, dialog, toast and the app bar get `backdrop-filter: blur(18px) saturate(1.3)`. This gives the \\\"frosted soft panels over the scene\\\".\\n  - `--radius` is 0.875rem and cards have a soft two-layer shadow (\\\"subtle depth\\\").\\n  - `--font-sans` is the system stack (\\\"system sans-serif\\\").\\n  - `.dark` and the night palette use deep indigo `#0b0f24` / `#0e1330` with a `#a5b4fc` accent (\\\"deep indigo for night\\\").\\n  - **The palette adapts to the scene.** Each scene has a `data-wx` key (`clear|hot|cloudy|rain|storm|snow|wind|fog` + `-day|-night`, plus `calm`). That key sets `--sky-a` / `--sky-b` for the background gradient, and sets `--primary`, `--primary-active`, `--ring` and `--primary-foreground` for the whole app: `hot-day` gets amber `#a54a08`, `rain-day` gets slate blue `#2f5b8a`, `storm-day` gets violet `#4f46a8`, `clear-night` gets indigo `#a5b4fc`, and so on (see \\\"Palettes\\\" in styles.css). Day scenes use the light neutral surface tokens and night scenes use the dark indigo ones. In the client, put `data-wx` on the app root and set it from the current city's weather code and its own sunrise and sunset. Do not use the viewer's clock.\\n  - `--pop` (chance-of-rain figures) is `#1f5f99` by day and `#9cc7f0` by night.\\n- Icons: lucide (cloud-rain, sun, moon, cloud, cloud-sun, cloud-moon, cloud-drizzle, cloud-lightning, snowflake, wind, cloud-fog, search, navigation, refresh-cw, bookmark, trash-2, wifi-off, alert-circle, map-pin-off, columns-2, download, home, sliders-vertical, plus, clock). The mockup draws them from an inline sprite.\\n\\n## App shell\\n\\n- Navigation: `Sidebar`, because there are five destinations. On Home, the places panel acts as a second side panel next to the main view (the \\\"side panel plus main view\\\" the concept asks for).\\n- Destinations, in order: Home (home), Search (search), Saved cities (bookmark), Compare (columns-2), Settings (sliders-vertical). No sections.\\n- Shell parts: product name \\\"Animated Weather\\\" in the `TopBar`, plus a search icon button on phones only. There is no `ThemeToggle`, because light or dark follows the scene (day or night at the shown city). There is no account.\\n- At 1280px: a 240px frosted sidebar, and Home shows the 280px places panel next to the main column. At 768px: the sidebar stays, and Home's places become a horizontal strip of chips above the main column (the side panel appears from 1200px). At 360px: the sidebar becomes a drawer opened by the menu button in the top bar, and every screen is a single column.\\n- The scene (`.scene`) is fixed, full screen and behind everything (`z-index: -1`). Every screen has one. Search, Saved cities and Settings show the current city's scene. Compare and the loading, denied and first-visit states show the neutral `calm` scene, so the per-city tints read clearly.\\n\\n## Tokens\\n\\nPaste these blocks into the client's global CSS after the\\n`@corbits/react-ui` theme import. Names match the kit, so `bg-background`,\\n`text-foreground`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`, `bg-primary`\\nand the other kit classes pick them up. The per-scene overrides (the 17 `[data-wx]` sky pairs and accent sets, and the day and night surface sets) live in styles.css under \\\"Sky colours\\\" and \\\"Palettes\\\". Port them as `[data-wx=\\\"…\\\"]` selectors on the app root.\\n\\n```css\\n:root {\\n  --background: #eef2f6;\\n  --foreground: #121820;\\n  --card: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.82);\\n  --card-foreground: #121820;\\n  --popover: #ffffff;\\n  --popover-foreground: #121820;\\n  --primary: #2f5b8a;\\n  --primary-foreground: #ffffff;\\n  --primary-active: #264b72;\\n  --secondary: rgb(18 24 32 / 0.06);\\n  --secondary-foreground: #121820;\\n  --muted: rgb(18 24 32 / 0.06);\\n  --muted-foreground: #46505e;\\n  --accent: rgb(18 24 32 / 0.08);\\n  --accent-foreground: #121820;\\n  --destructive: #a8322a;\\n  --destructive-foreground: #ffffff;\\n  --success: #cfe3d3;\\n  --success-foreground: #121820;\\n  --border: rgb(18 24 32 / 0.12);\\n  --input: #7b8594;\\n  --ring: #2f5b8a;\\n  --radius: 0.875rem;\\n  --radius-sm: calc(var(--radius) - 4px);\\n  --radius-lg: calc(var(--radius) + 4px);\\n  --shadow-popover: 0 12px 32px rgb(10 20 40 / 0.16), 0 1px 3px rgb(10 20 40 / 0.08);\\n  --font-sans: system-ui, -apple-system, \\\"Segoe UI\\\", Roboto, \\\"Helvetica Neue\\\", Arial, sans-serif;\\n  --font-mono: \\\"Space Mono\\\", \\\"Fira Code\\\", Monaco, Consolas, monospace;\\n  --ease-out: cubic-bezier(0.23, 1, 0.32, 1);\\n  --ease-in-out: cubic-bezier(0.65, 0, 0.35, 1);\\n  --duration-micro: 150ms;\\n  --duration-standard: 200ms;\\n  --duration-large: 300ms;\\n  color-scheme: light;\\n}\\n.dark {\\n  --background: #0b0f24;\\n  --foreground: #eef1fa;\\n  --card: rgb(18 23 52 / 0.74);\\n  --card-foreground: #eef1fa;\\n  --popover: #171c3d;\\n  --popover-foreground: #eef1fa;\\n  --primary: #a5b4fc;\\n  --primary-foreground: #0b1030;\\n  --primary-active: #c3cdfd;\\n  --secondary: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.1);\\n  --secondary-foreground: #eef1fa;\\n  --muted: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.08);\\n  --muted-foreground: #b6bdd6;\\n  --accent: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.12);\\n  --accent-foreground: #eef1fa;\\n  --destructive: #f08a80;\\n  --destructive-foreground: #0b0f24;\\n  --success: #2f5a45;\\n  --success-foreground: #eef1fa;\\n  --border: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.14);\\n  --input: #8b93b3;\\n  --ring: #a5b4fc;\\n  --shadow-popover: 0 12px 32px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.5);\\n  color-scheme: dark;\\n}\\n@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {\\n  :root:not(.dark):not(.light) {\\n    --background: #0b0f24;\\n    --foreground: #eef1fa;\\n    --card: rgb(18 23 52 / 0.74);\\n    --card-foreground: #eef1fa;\\n    --popover: #171c3d;\\n    --popover-foreground: #eef1fa;\\n    --primary: #a5b4fc;\\n    --primary-foreground: #0b1030;\\n    --primary-active: #c3cdfd;\\n    --secondary: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.1);\\n    --secondary-foreground: #eef1fa;\\n    --muted: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.08);\\n    --muted-foreground: #b6bdd6;\\n    --accent: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.12);\\n    --accent-foreground: #eef1fa;\\n    --destructive: #f08a80;\\n    --destructive-foreground: #0b0f24;\\n    --success: #2f5a45;\\n    --success-foreground: #eef1fa;\\n    --border: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.14);\\n    --input: #8b93b3;\\n    --ring: #a5b4fc;\\n    --shadow-popover: 0 12px 32px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.5);\\n    color-scheme: dark;\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n| Role                  | Token                | Tailwind class                       |\\n| --------------------- | -------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\\n| Page                  | `--background`       | `bg-background`                      |\\n| Text                  | `--foreground`       | `text-foreground`                    |\\n| Secondary text        | `--muted-foreground` | `text-muted-foreground`              |\\n| Divider               | `--border`           | `border-border`                      |\\n| Main action           | `--primary`          | `bg-primary text-primary-foreground` |\\n| Frosted panel         | `--card`             | `bg-card text-card-foreground`       |\\n| Stat tiles, chips     | `--muted`            | `bg-muted`                           |\\n| Error notice edge     | `--destructive`      | `border-destructive`                 |\\n| Scene sky, top/bottom | `--sky-a`, `--sky-b` | custom (scene only)                  |\\n| Chance of rain        | `--pop`              | custom                               |\\n\\nType scale: 12/16 (labels, small), 14/20 (body), 16/24 (hour temps), 18/28 (h2), 20/28 (condition), 30/36 (h1), 48 (compare temp), 64–96 clamp (current temperature, weight 250).\\nSpacing: 4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64px.\\nRadii, shadows and motion: the `--radius`, `--shadow-*`, `--duration-*` and\\n`--ease-*` tokens above. Scene change: 1200ms fade (`scene-in`).\\n\\n## Components\\n\\nEvery part maps to a `@corbits/react-ui` component from the react-ui skill.\\n\\n| Mockup class                  | Kit component                          | Used for                                       |\\n| ----------------------------- | -------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\\n| `.app-bar`, `.app-nav`        | `TopBar`, `Sidebar`, `SidebarItem`     | shell and navigation                           |\\n| `.button`                     | `Button`                               | primary actions (Refresh, Compare, Install)    |\\n| `.button-outline`             | `Button variant=\\\"outline\\\"`             | secondary actions (Save city, Use my location) |\\n| `.button-ghost`               | `Button variant=\\\"ghost\\\"`               | Edit, remove, icon buttons                     |\\n| `.input`                      | `Input`                                | city search box                                |\\n| `.card`                       | `Card`                                 | every frosted panel                            |\\n| `.stat-grid`                  | `StatGrid`                             | feels like, wind, humidity, high/low, rain, sun |\\n| `.unit-toggle .filter-chip`   | `FilterBar` / `FilterChip` (aria-pressed) | °C / °F                                     |\\n| `.switch`                     | `Switch`                               | Simpler effects                                |\\n| `.checkbox`                   | `Checkbox`                             | pick cities to compare                         |\\n| `.badge`                      | `Badge` (default, success, warning)    | scene text, Saved, Old, counts                 |\\n| `.skeleton`                   | `Skeleton`                             | loading placeholders                           |\\n| `.empty`                      | `EmptyState`                           | no results, no saved cities, first visit       |\\n| `.notice`                     | `Card` + `Alert` styling               | offline, error, location-denied messages       |\\n| `.dialog`                     | `Dialog`                               | Install app (sheet under 640px)                |\\n| `.toast`                      | `Toast` / `Toaster`                    | confirmations and Undo                         |\\n| `.scene`                      | custom `WeatherScene` (canvas)         | full-screen animated background                |\\n| `.wx-chip`, `.wx-band`, `.swatch` | custom, tinted by `data-wx`        | per-city weather tints                         |\\n| `.hours`, `.days`, `.place-list`, `.city-list`, `.cmp-grid` | layout lists | forecasts, places, compare grid           |\\n\\n## Screens\\n\\n### Home\\n\\n- Route: `/` (mockup `#/home`, plus a state name)\\n- Requirements: IR-1 (home screen), IR-6 (weather data), IR-8 (device location), IR-9 (last weather seen, saved choices); FR-1, FR-6, FR-7, FR-9, FR-12 to FR-16, FR-21 to FR-27, FR-32 to FR-35, FR-37, FR-38.\\n- Purpose: see the weather for where you are, or for the chosen city, at a glance.\\n- Layout, top to bottom: the full-screen `WeatherScene` behind everything. A places panel (`Card`): search entry, \\\"Your places\\\" list with chip, name, condition and temperature, and the \\\"Use my location\\\" button. Main column: header with the city name (h1), \\\"My location\\\", region, local time, the °C/°F toggle and **Refresh** (the primary action). Current conditions `Card`: big temperature, condition, one-line summary, and a `StatGrid` of feels like, wind (speed, direction, gusts), humidity, today's high and low, rain today and sunrise/sunset. Its footer shows the last-updated time, the scene `Badge` (for example \\\"Scene: Moderate rain, day\\\") and the Simpler effects `Switch`. Then the \\\"Next 24 hours\\\" strip (24 items: time, icon, temperature, chance of rain), then \\\"Next 7 days\\\" (day, icon and condition, chance of rain, low, range bar, high).\\n- Shows: temperatures as whole degrees with \\\"°\\\" and a true minus (−3°). Wind in km/h (or mph), rain in mm (or in). Times in 24-hour form at the city's local time. \\\"Updated 2 min ago\\\".\\n- 1280px: places panel on the left (sticky) and forecast column on the right. 768px: places as a horizontal scrolling strip above the column. 360px: single column; the places strip and hourly strip scroll sideways inside their own cards; the stat grid wraps to 2 columns.\\n- States:\\n  - populated (`#/home`): London, my location, moderate rain by day, slate blue.\\n  - Condition scenes: `#/home/hot` (Perth, hot day, amber), `#/home/cloudy` (Vancouver, overcast night), `#/home/storm` (Darwin, storm night, violet), `#/home/snow` (Oslo, heavy snow by day), `#/home/wind` (Cape Town, windy day, teal), `#/home/fog` (Milan, fog by day, grey), `#/home/night` (Sydney, clear night, deep indigo). Settings shows all 16 day and night swatches.\\n  - preview (`#/home/preview`): a search result that isn't saved yet (Springfield, light snow at night). A notice and a **Save city** button sit next to Refresh.\\n  - loading (`#/home/loading`): calm background; skeletons where the numbers go; Refresh disabled and reading \\\"Loading…\\\". Numbers always come before the scene (FR-32).\\n  - offline (`#/home/offline`): a notice reading \\\"You're offline.\\\" plus the age of the saved weather. \\\"Last updated today at 07:40\\\" and an \\\"Old: 3 hours\\\" warning badge. The figures stay visible. A city never seen before shows \\\"No saved weather for this city yet. Connect to the internet to see it.\\\"\\n  - error (`#/home/error`): a red-edged notice, \\\"We couldn't get fresh weather.\\\", with a **Try again** button. The older figures stay visible and are labelled \\\"Last updated 25 min ago\\\".\\n  - denied (`#/home/denied`): calm background; a \\\"Location is turned off for this app.\\\" notice with **Search for a city** and Try again; the saved places as a grid.\\n  - empty (`#/home/empty`), first visit with location declined and no saved cities: calm background; \\\"Find your weather\\\", **Search for a city**, and \\\"Use my location instead\\\".\\n- Test ids: `home-title`, `home-local-time`, `home-refresh-button`, `home-celsius-button`, `home-fahrenheit-button`, `home-temperature-count`, `home-feels-count`, `home-wind-count`, `home-humidity-count`, `home-high-low-count`, `home-rain-count`, `home-sun-count`, `home-updated-count`, `home-scene-badge`, `home-effects-checkbox`, `home-hours-list` (24 `li` rows), `home-days-list` (7 `li` rows), `home-search-link`, `home-edit-link`, `home-places-list`, `home-place-row`, `home-locate-button`, `home-save-button`, `home-preview-notice`, `home-offline-notice`, `home-old-badge`, `home-error-notice`, `home-retry-button`, `home-denied-notice`, `home-denied-search-link`, `home-denied-retry-button`, `home-empty-search-link`, `home-empty-locate-button`; states `home-populated`, `home-hot`, `home-cloudy`, `home-storm`, `home-snow`, `home-wind`, `home-fog`, `home-night`, `home-preview`, `home-loading`, `home-offline`, `home-error`, `home-denied`, `home-empty`.\\n\\n### Search\\n\\n- Route: `/search` (mockup `#/search`)\\n- Requirements: IR-2 (search with no-results and error states), IR-7 (city lookup); FR-2, FR-3, FR-8, FR-36.\\n- Purpose: find a city by name, tell same-named places apart, and open or save one.\\n- Layout, top to bottom: title \\\"Search\\\", then a `Card` with the `Input` (search type, autofocus) and a \\\"My location\\\" button. Then a results `Card`: a count line, then rows with weather chip, **name**, region and country, current temperature and condition, and a **Save** button (or a \\\"Saved\\\" badge if the city is already saved, FR-8). Tapping the row opens the city on Home (preview state).\\n- Shows: name, region, country (from the city lookup), and a temperature and condition for each result.\\n- 1280px and 768px: a 760px centred column. 360px: the same column; the temperature and condition move under the region.\\n- States:\\n  - populated: \\\"Springfield\\\" with 6 results.\\n  - empty (`#/search/empty`), no results: \\\"No results for “qzxwv”\\\" and \\\"Check the spelling, or try a larger city nearby. Small villages often appear under their nearest town.\\\" with Clear search.\\n  - loading (`#/search/loading`): 4 skeleton rows while typing (\\\"Lisb\\\").\\n  - error (`#/search/error`): \\\"Search isn't working right now.\\\" with Try again.\\n- Test ids: `search-title`, `search-input`, `search-locate-button`, `search-results-list`, `search-result-link`, `search-save-button`, `search-saved-badge`, `search-no-results`, `search-clear-link`, `search-error-notice`, `search-retry-button`.\\n\\n### Saved cities\\n\\n- Route: `/cities` (mockup `#/cities`)\\n- Requirements: IR-3 (saved list with temperature, condition, remove and compare selection), IR-9 (browser storage); FR-4, FR-5, FR-6, FR-7, NFR-14.\\n- Purpose: manage saved places, jump to one, and pick 2 to 4 to compare.\\n- Layout, top to bottom: title, a hint line, and **Compare 3 cities** (primary, a link to Compare). A count badge (\\\"3 picked · up to 4\\\") and \\\"Add a city\\\". Then the list `Card`, one row per city: compare `Checkbox`, weather chip, name (first row \\\"My location · London\\\"), condition and local time, region, temperature, and remove (trash). The My location row has a re-check location button instead of remove. Below the list, a note that cities are kept only in this browser.\\n- 1280px and 768px: a 760px centred column. 360px: the same rows; the text truncates with an ellipsis and never goes below 12px.\\n- States:\\n  - populated: 8 places, 3 ticked.\\n  - empty (`#/cities/empty`): \\\"No saved cities yet\\\", with copy and **Search for a city**.\\n- Test ids: `cities-title`, `cities-compare-link`, `cities-selected-count`, `cities-add-link`, `cities-list`, `cities-compare-checkbox`, `cities-city-link`, `cities-remove-button`, `cities-locate-button`, `cities-browser-note`, `cities-empty-card`, `cities-empty-search-link`.\\n\\n### Compare\\n\\n- Route: `/compare` (mockup `#/compare`)\\n- Requirements: IR-4 (side-by-side view of 2 to 4 cities); FR-17 to FR-20.\\n- Purpose: see 2 to 4 places side by side.\\n- Layout, top to bottom: title, the °C/°F toggle, and **Change cities** (primary, back to Saved cities). Then a grid of city `Card`s. Each card has a band tinted to its own weather (scene text and icon), name, region and local time, a large temperature, condition, a 2×2 list (feels like, wind, humidity, high/low), and a 4-step outlook (+1, +3, +6, +9 hours: time, icon, temperature).\\n- 1280px: 4 equal columns. 768px: cards at least 260px wide, scrolling sideways. 360px: one card at 82% of the screen width with the next one peeking, swiped sideways with snapping. This is the only screen that scrolls sideways, and only inside the grid.\\n- States:\\n  - populated: London, Perth, Oslo, Sydney.\\n  - empty (`#/compare/empty`): \\\"Pick at least two cities\\\" and **Choose cities**.\\n- Test ids: `compare-title`, `compare-celsius-button`, `compare-fahrenheit-button`, `compare-change-link`, `compare-grid`, `compare-card`, `compare-temperature-count`, `compare-empty-card`, `compare-pick-link`.\\n\\n### Settings\\n\\n- Route: `/settings` (mockup `#/settings`)\\n- Requirements: IR-5 (°C/°F, simpler effects, reduced-motion explanation, saved-in-browser note), IR-8, IR-9; FR-10, FR-11, FR-28, FR-30, FR-31, FR-39, NFR-14.\\n- Purpose: set units and effects, and understand motion, location and data.\\n- Layout, top to bottom: title and **Install app** (primary, opens the install `Dialog`). Units card with the toggle. Effects and motion card: the Simpler effects `Switch`, Reduced motion (read-only `Badge`, \\\"Your device: full motion\\\" or \\\"Your device: less motion\\\"), and Automatic smoothness (\\\"Always on\\\"). Location card with Use my location. \\\"Saved in this browser\\\" note. \\\"The scenes\\\" gallery: 16 swatches, each condition by day and by night. Credit line for Open-Meteo.\\n- 1280px and 768px: a 760px column. 360px: each setting's control wraps under its text.\\n- States: populated only.\\n- Test ids: `settings-title`, `settings-install-button`, `settings-celsius-button`, `settings-fahrenheit-button`, `settings-effects-checkbox`, `settings-motion-status`, `settings-locate-button`, `settings-browser-note`, `settings-scene-list`, `install-dialog`, `install-cancel-button`, `install-confirm-button`.\\n\\nShared test ids: `menu-button`, `app-name-link`, `top-search-link`, `nav-home-link`, `nav-search-link`, `nav-cities-link`, `nav-compare-link`, `nav-settings-link`, and toasts `toast-units`, `toast-refreshed`, `toast-locate`, `toast-locate-blocked`, `toast-saved`, `toast-removed`, `toast-undo-button`, `toast-undo`, `toast-retry`, `toast-install`.\\n\\n## Data\\n\\n- IR-6 Weather data: the Open-Meteo forecast service, with no key. One request per place returns current conditions, 24 hourly and 7 daily values, sunrise and sunset, and weather codes. Map each weather code to one of the 7 conditions plus an intensity (light, moderate or heavy). Day or night comes from that city's sunrise and sunset. Reuse responses for about 5 minutes (NFR-13). Refresh on demand, and on returning after 15 minutes or more away.\\n- IR-7 City lookup: Open-Meteo city search, called as the person types (300ms pause), returning name, region (admin1), country and coordinates. The list is kept in the order the service returns.\\n- IR-8 Device location: the browser's location feature. It is asked for only on first open and when the person taps \\\"Use my location\\\". If it's blocked, Home shows the denied state.\\n- IR-9 Browser storage: saved cities (name, region, country, coordinates), unit, simpler-effects choice, and the last weather seen per city with its time. The offline state uses that last weather.\\n\\n## Flows\\n\\n### F1 Check the weather where I am\\n\\n1. Open `/` for the first time; the browser asks for location.\\n2. Allow it: the loading state shows skeletons, the figures fill in, then the scene fades in to match (for example, rain by day).\\n3. Result: Home shows My location with current conditions, 24 hours and 7 days. If location is declined, the denied state appears (or the empty state on a first visit with nothing saved).\\n\\n### F2 Find and save a city\\n\\n1. On `/search`, type \\\"Springfield\\\": 6 results with region and country.\\n2. Tap \\\"Springfield, Illinois\\\": Home opens in the preview state with its scene (light snow, night).\\n3. Tap **Save city**: a toast confirms, and the city joins Your places. A city that's already saved shows \\\"Saved\\\" in search instead of Save.\\n\\n### F3 Compare cities\\n\\n1. On `/cities`, tick 2 to 4 cities. A fifth checkbox is disabled while 4 are ticked.\\n2. Tap **Compare 3 cities**.\\n3. Result: `/compare` shows the cards side by side, each tinted to its weather; on a phone, swipe through them.\\n\\n### F4 Make it calmer\\n\\n1. On `/settings`, turn on Simpler effects (or set reduce motion on the device).\\n2. Result: scenes use fewer particles (or hold still); the figures and layout are unchanged.\\n\\n## Interaction notes\\n\\n- °C/°F: one choice for the whole app (FR-10/11). It changes every temperature, wind (km/h ↔ mph) and rain (mm ↔ in), and is saved. The mockup only flips the pressed state and shows `toast-units`.\\n- Changing city cross-fades the scene for 1200ms with no blank flash (FR-26). The palette tokens change at the same time (300ms colour transition).\\n- Scene rendering: a canvas behind the content. At full quality there are many drops with splashes, snow in depth layers, moving cloud layers, lightning, heat shimmer and rolling mist. Heavier weather means more particles. The canvas measures its frame rate and steps quality down below about 30fps, and back up after it recovers. It stops when the tab is hidden. Under reduced motion the scene is still: sky colours plus static shapes, no lightning. Lightning never flashes more than 3 times a second (NFR-4). The mockup's CSS particles stand in for this. `.scene.lite` shows simpler effects and `.scene.calm` shows reduced motion.\\n- The scene is `aria-hidden`; its meaning is in the \\\"Scene: …\\\" badge. Hour and day rows give chance of rain and highs and lows as text for screen readers. Notices use `role=\\\"status\\\"`, and errors use `role=\\\"alert\\\"`.\\n- Removing a city happens at once, with a toast and **Undo** for 4000ms (no confirm dialog).\\n- Shared loading pattern: skeletons where figures go, with the layout kept. Shared error pattern: a red-edged notice with Try again, and any older data stays visible with its age.\\n- Contrast: every text sits on a frosted `--card` panel (82% white by day, 74% indigo by night), so it meets 4.5:1 over every scene.\\n- Keyboard: tab order runs top bar, sidebar, places panel, header controls, then content. The hourly strip and compare grid are focusable and scroll with the arrow keys.\\n- Install (FR-39): the app ships a web app manifest. \\\"Install app\\\" opens a dialog, and Install triggers the browser's own install prompt.\\n\"}"}}]},"finish_reason":null}]}

data: {"choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{},"finish_reason":"tool_calls"}]}

data: {"choices":[],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":120,"completion_tokens":60}}

data: [DONE]

